===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|göu|lang=gmh}}, {{term|gou|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|gawi|lang=goh}}, {{term|gouwi|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*gawi}} (compare Low German {{term|Gohe|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|gouw|lang=nl}}, West Frisian {{term|gea|lang=fy}}, {{term|goa|lang=fy}}), from earlier {{term/t|de|*gaawja}} ‘riverlands, lakeside land’, from collective {{term/t|gem-pro|*ga-}} + {{term/t|gem-pro|*awjō}} ‘land by a waterway’ (compare German {{term|Aue|lang=de}}).

